{"name":"Regent Grey","hex":"#798488","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"regent","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who rules in place of the monarch, especially because the monarch is too young, absent, or disabled. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Any ruler."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Ruling; governing; regnant.","Exercising vicarious authority."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regent"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Regent","blocks":[{"text":"In a monarchy, a regent is a person appointed to execute the office of a monarch temporarily, essentially as a substitute ruler. Regencies may arise for a number of reasons, including the monarch being a minor, ill, absent from the country, or otherwise unavailable. A regent may also be appointed in cases where the throne is vacant, or the identity of the legitimate monarch is disputed. The rule of a regent or regents is called a regency."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Sture_Sten_Svantesson_d.y._1492-1520%2C_och_Kristina_Gyllenstierna%2C_1494-1559_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15066.tif/lossless-page1-330px-Sture_Sten_Svantesson_d.y._1492-1520%2C_och_Kristina_Gyllenstierna%2C_1494-1559_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15066.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regent"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1